WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.935
-Thank you very much, everybody.

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.836
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.271
Well, guys, last night

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.273
President Trump held
a press conference

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.275
and this one was out there,
even for him.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.277
I mean, when Time-Life
releases a box set

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.813
of Trump's craziest moments,
this will be on it.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.381
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:16.783
Trump was asked to commit

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.018
to a peaceful transition
of power,

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.855
if he loses the election,
and this was his response.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.761 line:0%
-Well, we're gonna have
to see what happens.

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.963
You know that I've been
complaining very strongly

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:34.233
about the ballots
and the ballots are a disaster.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.802
We wanna have --
Get rid of the ballots

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.604
and you'll have a very transf--
we'll have very peaceful --

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.106
There won't be a transfer,
frankly,

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.608
[ Laughter ]
There'll be a continuation.

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.942
-Whoa.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.944
-So, if Trump loses
the election,

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.379
getting him
out of the White House

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.548
will be like trying to get
a bird out of your living room.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.815
[ Laughter ]
It's like, "Oh...no.

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.150
I got him.
Hold on! Okay.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.319
Nobody move! He's --
He's behind the curtain!

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.154
Nobody move!
Shut the door! Shut the door!

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.722
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:58.457
I'm getting the feeling
this year is gonna end

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:00.293
with Trump locking himself
in the Oval Office

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.494
while yelling in the phone...

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.363
[ As Trump ]
Space Force, attack!

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:06.032
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.200
Even with five extra people,
it sounds fantastic.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.269
I will take it.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.004
[ Applause ]
I love you. I love you.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.573
Safe, distanced,

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:16.676
distanced, socially distanced,
everyone is safe, but, man,

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.876
it feels good.

00:01:17.876 --> 00:01:19.813
It feels great, actually.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.047
[ Cheering, laughter,
and applause ]

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.550
Ah! I'm so happy right now.
I just wanna --

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.551
Let's roll the credits.
The show's over.

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:27.253
I'm happy.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.888
Bye, everybody.
Take care.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:33.993
♪♪

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.127
Ah!

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.563
The peaceful transfer
of power is

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:39.898
one of the pillars
of our democracy

00:01:39.898 --> 00:01:42.701
and Trump treats it like
a brunch he might bail on.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.470
[ Laughter ]
[ As Trump ] Game time decision.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.105
I have to see
how my day's going.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:47.740
I'm not sure.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.475
I do love a little
eggs Benny, though.

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:52.111
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:53.312
After Trump's comments,

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:55.081
Senate Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell tried

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.483
to assure people
that things would be okay.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.651
He tweeted...

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.692
And, if recent news
has taught us anything,

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:07.860
it's that you can always count

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.529
on Mitch McConnell
to keep his word.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:10.797
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.897
-Ooh!

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.400
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.135
-Seriously, even though
the Republicans were like,

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.170
"Mitch, please."

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.338
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:20.540
Later in the press conference,

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.242
a reporter asked Trump
about Meghan Markle

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.144
basically supporting Joe Biden,

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:27.079 line:0%
and this is what he had
to say about her.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:28.848 line:0%
-I'm not a fan of hers.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.283 line:0%
And she probably
has heard that.

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:35.221 line:0%
But I wish a lot of luck

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.389 line:0%
to Harry

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.957 line:0%
-Oh!
-'cause he's gonna need it.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.259
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, God.

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.526
-Wow!

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:42.161
Who had Meghan Markle
on their random

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.930
Trump Insults Bingo card,
anyone?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.264
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.432
If you're keeping track,
Meghan Markle's got beef

00:02:47.432 --> 00:02:48.568
with the queen of England

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.769
and the president
of the United States.

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:52.472
She's just one Jay-Z fight away

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.307
from taking on
the entire Illuminati.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:57.510
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.378
After that, Trump was
answering a question

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:01.113
about the coronavirus vaccine

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:03.515
when he used a made-up excuse
to get out of there.

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:04.517 line:0%
[ Laughing ]
Watch this.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.785 line:0%
-Ultimately,
the White House has

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.887 line:0%
to approve it and...

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.555 line:0%
maybe we will
and maybe we won't,

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:10.990 line:0%
but we'll be taking a look.
-Mr. President.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:14.093 line:0%
-I have to leave
for an emergency phone call.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.796 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
I'm gonna let Scott
and Larry finish up.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.966
-That's right. That's right.
Trump was like...

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.101
[ As Trump ]
Uh, yeah, what's
the emergency, what, what?

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.803
Everything I just said
at this press conference?

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.371
Okay, yeah, bye.

00:03:26.371 --> 00:03:28.141
Hey, listen to this.
Earlier today, it was announced

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.076
that Russian
President Vladimir Putin

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:32.745
was nominated for the
[ Laughing ] Nobel Peace Prize.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:35.448
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.716
Yep.
Putin is thrilled,

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:39.052
while everyone else
in the category is poisoned.

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:41.754
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.756
First Trump, then Putin?

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.191
Right now, Kim Jong-un
is standing

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:47.560
by a tin can on a string like,
"Any second now...

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.861
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.663
Any second now."

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.331
Well, guys, Halloween is
just around the corner,

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:53.833
but, this week,
the CDC announced

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:57.202
that no one should have
Halloween parties.

00:03:57.202 --> 00:03:58.705
-[ Groaning ]
-Yeah. It's a huge bummer.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.673
It almost feels like
the CDC knows it, too.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.643
I mean, check out the PSA
that they released today.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:06.979
-We at the CDC are here to guide
you through the COVID pandemic,

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:09.148
which is why we're announcing,
come October...

00:04:10.649 --> 00:04:12.285
...should take place.
None.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.420 line:0%
Not even our own
office Halloween party,

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.522 line:0%
which is downright sick.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.125
I mean, this party is
off. the. hook.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.392
We've got fog.

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:21.660
We've got a DJ.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.863
We've got Anthony Fauci
as Batman,

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.564
entering on a zip line?

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:28.567
It was so 2019.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.002
It was a different time.

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:33.105
And, this fall, we all have
a collective responsibility

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:35.108
to not recreate last year.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:38.110
No matter how lit. it. was.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.012
[ Laughter ]
This party is legendary.

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:41.581
Last year, Brenda from Genetics

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.916
dressed
as Streptococcus pneumoniae.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.451
Take that, Heidi Klum!

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.086
You can't control this banger,

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:48.454
but you can control

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.855
the virus.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:51.857
So just be safe.
Stay inside.

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:53.058
Rewatch "Tiger King."

00:04:53.058 --> 00:04:54.794
I mean, okay.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.395
Can you imagine
the costumes, though?

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:59.465
Bret in Lab Safety was gonna
bring an actual tiger.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.434
-[ Growl ]
-And you think we couldn't
top last year?

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:04.203
Tell that to our hologram
Joseph Walter Mountin.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.406
He founded the CDC, bitch!

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.707
God, I'm gonna miss this party.
God!

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:11.643 line:0%
CDC.

00:05:11.643 --> 00:05:12.844 line:0%
Wear your mask.

00:05:12.844 --> 00:05:17.817
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.952
-Unfortunately, Halloween
isn't the only celebration

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.420
that's being affected
by the pandemic.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.423 line:0%
It looks like New Year's Eve
is gonna be different, too.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:27.025 line:0%
-For the first time
in 114 years,

00:05:27.025 --> 00:05:29.261 line:0%
there's gonna be no crowd,
no revelers, allowed

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:30.362 line:0%
in Times Square.
-[ Sighs heavily ]

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:31.831 line:0%
-Organizers announcing

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.899 line:0%
a new virtually enhanced event

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:38.170 line:0%
with live components that
incorporate social distancing.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.205
-Yeah. And, if you're upset
you can't go

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:42.074
to Times Square
on New Year's Eve,

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:43.509
then I'm pretty sure
you've never been

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.444
to Times Square
on New Year's Eve.

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:47.980
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.414
Virtual, not virtual.

00:05:49.414 --> 00:05:50.716
Live, pretaped.

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:51.917
It doesn't matter.

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:54.187
Just get us the hell
out of 2020, please!

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.221
[ Laughter and applause ]
Carson, just say it!

00:05:56.221 --> 00:06:00.426
Just say it now, and we'll
all agree it's New Year's.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.361
Meanwhile, Planet Fitness
is like, "Damn,

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:05.131
what the hell are we gonna do
with 10,000 purple top hats?"

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:08.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:11.237
[ Clap ]

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.338
Well, this is fun.

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:13.906
The company that makes emojis

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.375
just announced 217 new ones.

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:18.544
Most of them are variations
on existing emojis,

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.212
but some of them
are pretty surprising.

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:21.780
Here, take a look.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.182
First one is called...

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:27.286 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
This next one is called...

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:32.825 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:35.561 line:0%
[ Slaps leg ]

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:37.095
Takis.
-Yeah.

00:06:37.095 --> 00:06:39.665 line:0%
-This one is called...

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.600 line:0%
That's fun.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.069 line:0%
And, finally, this new emoji
is called...

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:45.070 line:0%
-Oh!
-There you go.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:47.139 line:0%
[ Smattering of applause ]
And now,

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:50.009
quickly changing pace a little,
here's a new segment, called

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:52.244
"How Was That Legal Until Now??"

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:56.982
♪♪

00:06:56.982 --> 00:07:01.220 line:0%
-The MTA today officially
changed its rules to prohibit

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.756 line:0%
defecating on subways and buses.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:05.691
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.759
-Whoa! Wait.

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:08.828
[ Laughter ]
Wait.

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:11.330
Wait, wait.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.932
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:16.235
Wait.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.003
[ Laughter ]
Wait.

00:07:18.003 --> 00:07:19.405
You mean, all this time...

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:22.308
[ Laughter ]
-I know. I can't.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:23.375
Just ruined my weekend.

00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:26.178
I mean, just ruined it.

00:07:26.178 --> 00:07:28.080
Wow!

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.116
And, finally,
here's some exciting...

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:31.551
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.551 --> 00:07:34.287
news about a 96-year-old woman
in Pennsylvania.

00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:35.287
Watch this.

00:07:35.287 --> 00:07:36.822 line:0%
-A 96-year-old.

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:38.958 line:0%
Meet Sarah in Pittsburgh,
who is still one of the best

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.892 line:0%
when it comes
to knocking down pins.

00:07:40.892 --> 00:07:42.761 line:0%
She became the first
at her local bowling alley

00:07:42.761 --> 00:07:44.463 line:0%
to bowl a perfect game.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:45.764
-That's amazing.

00:07:45.764 --> 00:07:48.034
When most 96-year-olds bowl,
they go down the alley

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:49.735
with the ball.
[ Laughter ]

